                <pb facs="0288" n="288" sameAs="frus:frus1861/pg288"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of State
                        to Mr. Schurz</hi>.</head>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">[Extract.]</note>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 46.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of
                            State</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-11-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 5, 1861</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your despatch of September 2 (No. 13) was
                    duly received.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am gratified to learn that the public opinion around you is less injurious than
                    formerly. I trust that it is the beginning of a better understanding in Europe
                    of the real character and determination of the American people.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>F. W. SEWARD,</signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary</hi>.</closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carl Schurz</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c., Madrid</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
